00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Grand Piano is a 2013 Spanish English-language thriller film directed by Eugenio Mira,
written by Damien Chazelle, and starring Elijah Wood and John Cusack.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film is about a once-promising pianist returning for a comeback performance, only to
be the target of a sniper who will kill him if he plays one wrong note.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The film premiered at Fantastic Fest on 20 September 2013 and
was given a VOD release on 30 January 2014.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It was given a limited release in American theatres on 7 March.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Grand Piano was Alex Winter's first non-cameo film role since 1993's Freaked.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois, sniper,
threat of death, stage fright, live performance.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
